WEBVTT

00:00:02.330 --> 00:00:05.760
Looking at the Anime Club's 
school festival plans...

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:07.230
What do you think you're doing?!

00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:09.390
An anime screening, huh?

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:13.160
Although the student council president 
is close with the anime club president.

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:15.240
I guess it's no use protesting.

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:30.500
I could never figure it out.

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:34.250
So I finally asked Senpai, and it turns out, 
it's the word for the back of your knee!

00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:36.010
What?! Amazing!

00:02:06.890 --> 00:02:08.780
Hello.

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:10.830
Whoa, it's the Production Committee.

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:12.020
Student council!

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:14.690
Are you occupied right now?

00:02:16.690 --> 00:02:19.660
Did Arisu-chan use a ton of club funds again?

00:02:19.890 --> 00:02:21.950
What do you mean by "again"?

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:22.960
Not this time.

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:24.410
Not <i>this</i> time?!

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:27.840
The president submitted a proposal 
for the school festival, but...

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:28.910
Go ahead.

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:32.930
"An anime screening? I can't approve."

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:34.920
...is what the council president said.

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:36.340
You sound nothing like her.

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:39.270
Arts clubs are required to present 
something at the school festival,

00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:41.930
in part, to demonstrate what 
they've been working on.

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:45.210
Unless you can show off something 
impressive for the Anime Club,

00:02:45.210 --> 00:02:47.180
I won't let you participate.

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:54.060
So why can't we have an anime screening 
to show off the Anime Club's activities?

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:56.070
Let me talk to Tsubaki.

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:57.840
The president won't be meeting with you.

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:00.450
If you can't present anything, 
the club will be shut down.

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:04.450
Shut down again?!

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:16.280
What should we do?

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:17.810
We have to do it.

00:03:17.810 --> 00:03:20.370
We need to come up with an 
idea for something to present,

00:03:20.370 --> 00:03:21.700
or we're getting shut down.

00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:27.100
Shall we write a doujinshi or something?

00:03:27.320 --> 00:03:30.100
How about a concert?

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:34.860
A presentation of the special ability 
battle anime concepts I came up with.

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:38.360
How about we invite voice actors, 
and hold a public radio recording?

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:40.360
That's too bourgeoisie.

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:45.620
I know, how about we make an anime together?

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:57.180
Minoacchi, do you have any idea how 
much work it is to make an anime?

00:03:57.830 --> 00:03:59.250
It is?

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:02.460
Scripts, storyboards, artwork, recording...

00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:04.760
It takes a lot of people.

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:09.900
Not even my Swiss bank account 
could cover the production cost.

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:11.770
Good for you and your imaginary bank account.

00:04:12.250 --> 00:04:13.670
But I...

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:19.090
want to accomplish something 
with the Anime Club.

00:04:19.090 --> 00:04:22.900
I want to show them something 
that the Anime Club has done.

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:25.910
I appreciate your sentiment, Minoa.

00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:36.540
This is the power of <i>real</i> money.

00:04:36.690 --> 00:04:38.920
So you really were a bourgeoisie.

00:04:39.110 --> 00:04:40.930
I'm on board.

00:04:40.930 --> 00:04:44.430
Making our own anime sounds exciting.

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:45.850
Erika-senpai!

00:04:47.930 --> 00:04:49.130
All right, fine.

00:04:49.130 --> 00:04:51.930
However... we aren't using this money.

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:56.190
How are we going to make one, then?

00:04:56.440 --> 00:05:00.270
There are plenty of things we can do, 
like asking other clubs for help.

00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:02.340
We have three months until 
the school festival.

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:05.070
Let's make an anime with our own hands.

00:05:06.550 --> 00:05:07.410
Okay.

00:05:13.450 --> 00:05:14.960
Anime Club Original Anime
Project Meeting!

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:16.710
First, we need a project idea.

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:18.580
Have you all brought yours?

00:05:18.780 --> 00:05:21.960
I propose an orthodox idol anime.

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:26.090
Anime Proposal

00:05:22.410 --> 00:05:26.470
There'll be a heated battle at 
the school festival concert,

00:05:26.470 --> 00:05:29.600
competing with the best music and dance.

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:33.470
<b>"Schwein of Ockstadt"</b>

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:33.470
<b>Concept 1</b>

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:33.470
If you want passion, mine is even hotter.

00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:42.980
Special Attacks

00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:42.980
Main Weapon

00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:42.980
Ragnablade

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:37.440
The protagonist is me, Mad King Kai.

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:39.900
My family develops the most powerful 
attack spell in the world,

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:42.980
Amethyst Extra Circulation!

00:05:43.170 --> 00:05:45.490
I came up with a magic girl anime.

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:49.960
Girls love transformation 
and magic, after all.

00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:52.740
Even <i>PreFae</i> is getting into magic this year.

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:57.500
I came up with something from 
the anime I saw as a kid.

00:05:57.730 --> 00:06:00.000
The protagonist, separated from their parents,

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:03.230
uses magic, transforms, pilots robots,

00:06:03.230 --> 00:06:06.760
and after a lot of suffering, 
is reunited with their mother.

00:06:07.040 --> 00:06:09.400
In the last episode, 
they're greeted to heaven,

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:12.260
and the audience is moved to tears, too.

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:18.020
Anime Club Original Anime
Planning Meeting!

00:06:12.490 --> 00:06:14.690
How many do you intend to make?

00:06:14.690 --> 00:06:15.700
Uh...

00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:16.710
Like a year?

00:06:16.710 --> 00:06:18.020
Won't happen.

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:25.900
Anime Club Original Anime
Planning Meeting!

00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:19.770
Sheesh.

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:24.270
None of these ideas seem within 
reach for a group of students.

00:06:24.270 --> 00:06:25.200
Sebas.

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:30.160
<b>Supreme Production Commander</b>

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:30.160
<b>Kamiigusa Arisu</b>

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:33.660
<b>Supreme Production Commander
Kamiigusa Arisu</b>

00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:32.220
Supreme Production Commander,

00:06:32.220 --> 00:06:33.660
Kamiigusa Arisu.

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:37.790
It is the Galactic Era.

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:37.790
<b>It is the Galactic Era</b>

00:06:39.790 --> 00:06:43.540
<b>A super robot saves the world 
with love, passion and money.</b>

00:06:39.940 --> 00:06:43.540
A super robot saves the world 
with love, passion and money.

00:06:45.050 --> 00:06:46.550
<b>Super warrior</b>

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:46.550
Super warrior

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:49.050
<b>Arisuborg</b>

00:06:47.690 --> 00:06:49.050
Arisuborg

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:51.300
Alpha!

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:51.300
<b>Alpha!</b>

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:55.310
<b>Arisuborg-ɑ</b>

00:06:55.860 --> 00:06:57.970
You will see the tears of money.

00:06:58.890 --> 00:07:01.990
Yours sounds the most unrealistic.

00:07:01.990 --> 00:07:03.340
That was amazing.

00:07:03.340 --> 00:07:05.070
Who made that?

00:07:05.270 --> 00:07:09.010
Sebas did the script, storyboards, key art, 
backgrounds, photography, editing,

00:07:09.010 --> 00:07:10.990
all by himself, all in one night.

00:07:10.990 --> 00:07:14.330
Why don't we just let Sebas do everything?

00:07:15.790 --> 00:07:21.230
This may all be way too much for 
high schoolers to do by ourselves.

00:07:21.230 --> 00:07:22.710
Oh, have you forgotten

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:26.210
about the Anime Club's most 
well-read, intellectual

00:07:26.980 --> 00:07:29.210
Kouenji Miko?

00:07:29.680 --> 00:07:32.440
My proposal is for an alternate 
world summoner story.

00:07:32.970 --> 00:07:35.720
There's no way we'll be able to do all that.

00:07:35.860 --> 00:07:38.100
It'll be three minutes long.

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:40.290
I see, an anime short.

00:07:40.290 --> 00:07:42.600
Right, that's one option.

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:45.110
An anime short?

00:07:45.110 --> 00:07:48.550
There are many three-minute 
and five-minute long anime,

00:07:48.550 --> 00:07:52.020
since anime budgets and production 
time are in short supply these days.

00:07:52.020 --> 00:07:53.860
Those are anime shorts.

00:07:54.220 --> 00:07:55.450
In <i>Yasuda and Iwakura</i>,

00:07:55.450 --> 00:07:58.540
they use the same 30-second shot in every minute-and-a-half episode,

00:07:58.540 --> 00:08:02.870
while the screenwriter worked really 
hard each episode to write to length.

00:08:02.870 --> 00:08:05.600
There are lighter anime, like <i>Immun-kun</i>,

00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:08.750
which are targeted at a broader 
audience beyond just anime fans.

00:08:08.750 --> 00:08:11.810
In <i>Malcom Gakuen</i>, they hired a 
ton of high-profile voice actors

00:08:11.810 --> 00:08:14.800
from the original games 
for a really short anime,

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:18.140
and earned a reputation for being 
a complete waste of voice talent.

00:08:18.140 --> 00:08:20.980
<i>What's Up, Girl ZOO!</i>, also known as <i>Whagzoo</i>

00:08:20.980 --> 00:08:22.830
shows a character dying in each episode,

00:08:22.830 --> 00:08:24.790
despite being an idol anime spin-off.

00:08:24.790 --> 00:08:27.150
It's popular among fans of crazy anime.

00:08:27.480 --> 00:08:32.170
They stuff as much ideas and content 
as they can into a limited time span.

00:08:32.170 --> 00:08:34.910
It's amazing how satisfying they are.

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:38.910
I also like how convenient it is to 
watch them online with your smartphone.

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:41.140
It's easy to get through them, too.

00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:43.470
It's settled.

00:08:43.470 --> 00:08:46.420
Mikocchi, could you start on 
the screenplay right away?

00:08:46.600 --> 00:08:47.580
Got it.

00:08:47.580 --> 00:08:50.170
An anime short script is a piece of cake.

00:08:52.670 --> 00:08:55.300
<b>First Script Meeting</b>

00:08:52.670 --> 00:08:55.300
Let's begin the script meeting.

00:08:55.640 --> 00:08:56.970
It's a pleasure to work with you all.

00:08:59.280 --> 00:09:03.280
The protagonist walks into a shopping 
center door, and it's an alternate world?

00:09:03.280 --> 00:09:04.690
Is that interesting at all?

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:08.010
The first issue in any alternate 
world story is food.

00:09:08.010 --> 00:09:10.070
Who even cares?

00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:13.570
<b>Fourth Script Meeting</b>

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:15.820
I definitely want a moving scene.

00:09:17.570 --> 00:09:19.330
<b>Eighth Script Meeting</b>

00:09:19.330 --> 00:09:21.080
We'll need a transformation scene.

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:23.580
<b>Thirteenth Script Meeting</b>

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:24.850
About this scene...

00:09:24.850 --> 00:09:27.850
I came up with a concept for a way 
more spectacular special ability.

00:09:27.850 --> 00:09:29.710
I wrote alternate dialogue, too.

00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:32.210
<b>28th Script Meeting</b>

00:09:32.410 --> 00:09:34.910
It's missing a mid-story climax.

00:09:34.910 --> 00:09:36.220
Let's have a concert scene.

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:39.720
<b>45th Script Meeting</b>

00:09:40.070 --> 00:09:42.250
Where do the commercials go?

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:44.370
For an anime short?

00:09:44.370 --> 00:09:46.510
I think it would be funny.

00:09:46.510 --> 00:09:48.980
Like, bam, like in the middle of the story.

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:53.980
<b>Miko Quits Writing</b>

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:01.950
<b>53rd Script Meeting</b>

00:10:01.950 --> 00:10:04.330
Lunch break's going to end soon.

00:10:04.690 --> 00:10:06.680
We're kind of stuck.

00:10:06.680 --> 00:10:09.080
We underestimated anime shorts.

00:10:09.320 --> 00:10:13.090
It's actually pretty hard making 
a short show interesting.

00:10:15.090 --> 00:10:19.750
Hey, Mikocchi, we still haven't come up 
with any ideas after all this discussion.

00:10:19.750 --> 00:10:23.170
I don't think it's a problem with the 
dialogue or anything minor like that.

00:10:24.300 --> 00:10:27.600
Why don't we go back to the drawing board?

00:10:27.940 --> 00:10:31.000
The drawing board?

00:10:31.810 --> 00:10:34.110
Think it over from the top.

00:10:35.990 --> 00:10:38.620
The first one was the best.

00:10:38.620 --> 00:10:41.950
Let's change it back. Have
it done by after school today.

00:10:42.870 --> 00:10:45.870
I'm sick of you ordering me around.

00:10:45.870 --> 00:10:50.120
Do you have any idea how much work it 
is to write from scratch, you jerk?!

00:10:50.590 --> 00:10:53.130
I don't care, figure it out yourselves!

00:10:53.590 --> 00:10:55.110
The scriptwriter's down.

00:10:55.110 --> 00:10:57.130
Anime production problems.

00:10:58.060 --> 00:11:02.260
Don't stop me, let me sleep!

00:11:03.160 --> 00:11:04.260
No, I'm sleeping!

00:11:04.590 --> 00:11:05.100
Now!

00:11:05.100 --> 00:11:06.270
Here!

00:11:07.390 --> 00:11:09.270
Ow...

00:11:24.640 --> 00:11:27.480
They're image boards for anime.

00:11:30.520 --> 00:11:34.290
<i>"Don't... open... it"?</i>

00:11:34.620 --> 00:11:36.300
<i>I'm... sor... ry.</i>

00:11:36.490 --> 00:11:40.300
It looks like something that the 
old Anime Club members drew.

00:11:40.450 --> 00:11:42.800
The concept is a complete mess.

00:11:42.800 --> 00:11:45.550
But they have everything we like.

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:49.560
This is...

00:11:50.710 --> 00:11:53.190
A lot like the anime I saw a long time ago.

00:11:53.190 --> 00:11:58.420
That anime I saw as a kid was a complete 
mess, too, but it was really interesting.

00:11:58.420 --> 00:12:00.190
Oh, the one you were talking about.

00:12:00.350 --> 00:12:04.200
I think it'll be fun if we each made our 
own characters and have our own voice.

00:12:04.470 --> 00:12:06.180
Let's do this.

00:12:06.180 --> 00:12:07.790
I see.

00:12:07.790 --> 00:12:09.700
Can you do the script, Mikocchi?

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:11.330
Nope.

00:12:11.870 --> 00:12:14.340
Come on, chan-Miko!

00:12:14.340 --> 00:12:17.590
You're the only one who can write.

00:12:17.780 --> 00:12:20.570
You read a ton, you write fast,

00:12:20.570 --> 00:12:24.250
and you always put up with all our revisions.

00:12:26.870 --> 00:12:28.640
She's a producer.

00:12:28.640 --> 00:12:29.970
She's a producer.

00:12:30.390 --> 00:12:33.000
Okay, so I'm the producer.

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:35.100
Why don't we decide on everyone's roles?

00:12:35.470 --> 00:12:37.730
I'll be the character designer.

00:12:38.010 --> 00:12:40.860
I can do all the digital production.

00:12:41.080 --> 00:12:42.820
I'll do the audio work.

00:12:43.100 --> 00:12:45.950
I guess Gomon-sensei can be 
the production assistant.

00:12:48.700 --> 00:12:51.120
U-Uh, what about me?

00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:53.720
There's something only you can do, Minoacchi.

00:12:53.720 --> 00:12:56.580
Oh, right, like taking out the trash.

00:12:57.000 --> 00:12:58.210
You're the director.

00:12:58.650 --> 00:13:00.590
D-Director?

00:13:00.590 --> 00:13:02.690
You're the one who came up with the idea.

00:13:03.260 --> 00:13:07.560
Write up the story with Mikocchi, and once 
you have a script, draw the storyboards.

00:13:09.020 --> 00:13:12.110
What's a storyboard?

00:13:21.230 --> 00:13:22.110
<b>Final</b>

00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:24.960
Take it from here.

00:13:24.960 --> 00:13:26.110
Good work.

00:13:26.340 --> 00:13:28.480
Uh, what do I do?

00:13:28.480 --> 00:13:29.750
A storyboard?

00:13:29.750 --> 00:13:32.240
A storyboard is an anime's blueprint.

00:13:32.240 --> 00:13:34.630
You take the script, and draw up the specifics

00:13:34.630 --> 00:13:37.370
on things like settings, atmosphere, 
and character actions.

00:13:37.630 --> 00:13:40.130
You should take a look at other anime.

00:13:37.750 --> 00:13:40.130
<b>Gekigenki G</b>

00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:41.620
O-Okay.

00:13:42.200 --> 00:13:44.130
I'll see what I can do.

00:13:46.380 --> 00:13:48.390
Mii-chan, bath's ready.

00:13:49.060 --> 00:13:50.780
I'll take a bath later.

00:13:50.780 --> 00:13:51.930
What's up?

00:13:51.930 --> 00:13:56.520
My club's making an anime, so I'm 
looking for storyboard references.

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:56.520
Punch scene
Make the hand big

00:13:58.120 --> 00:14:00.140
Let me know if there's 
anything I can help with.

00:14:00.140 --> 00:14:03.380
Oh, we don't have a voice 
actress for Cute Girl A.

00:14:03.380 --> 00:14:05.440
Can I ask you to do it?

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:06.500
Cute girl?

00:14:06.500 --> 00:14:07.450
Sure!

00:14:07.450 --> 00:14:10.180
Now I just need Man A...

00:14:11.210 --> 00:14:12.300
Dad, are you sick?

00:14:12.300 --> 00:14:14.500
N-No, it's nothing.

00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:17.790
Scene | Visual | Content

00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:17.870
Cute Girl A cries
to Man A.

00:14:17.870 --> 00:14:19.210
Magical Erika: "Heh, So long as your 
RoboArisu is down, you have
no chance of defeating me!"

00:14:19.250 --> 00:14:20.710
Idol Kouki enters from 
the left. He's sparkly.

00:14:20.710 --> 00:14:22.290
Idol Kouki smiles. Idol Kouki: 
"You've got this! I'm here for you!"

00:14:21.170 --> 00:14:22.290
Yuirin enters from the right.

00:14:24.790 --> 00:14:26.760
You deleted the dialogue there?

00:14:27.830 --> 00:14:28.920
S-Sorry.

00:14:28.920 --> 00:14:31.150
It got too long with the action there.

00:14:31.150 --> 00:14:34.370
No one wants script writers.

00:14:34.830 --> 00:14:37.560
I will... I'll do my best to include it, okay?

00:14:38.930 --> 00:14:41.250
The character design is coming along, too.

00:14:41.250 --> 00:14:44.840
I definitely have to be super gorgeous.

00:14:45.990 --> 00:14:47.480
You have too many lines.

00:14:47.480 --> 00:14:49.220
We can't animate this.

00:14:49.220 --> 00:14:50.160
Fix it.

00:14:51.700 --> 00:14:54.700
Anime Club
Asagaya Minoa

00:14:53.830 --> 00:14:54.700
<b>Final</b>

00:14:54.700 --> 00:14:57.100
Take it from here.

00:14:57.100 --> 00:14:58.210
Good work.

00:14:59.510 --> 00:15:01.640
I feel like it's been changed a lot.

00:15:01.640 --> 00:15:02.960
I don't know.

00:15:02.960 --> 00:15:05.310
Come on, chan-Miko.

00:15:05.310 --> 00:15:07.990
Minoacchi's doing her best 
to make it interesting.

00:15:07.990 --> 00:15:10.540
This'll look good on your resume, too.

00:15:11.250 --> 00:15:11.890
Right.

00:15:11.890 --> 00:15:12.980
Are we good?

00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:17.470
Okay, let's get this done.

00:15:26.730 --> 00:15:30.240
<b>Anime Club
Original Animation Project</b>

00:15:26.730 --> 00:15:30.240
Urgently Needed!!
Cute Girl A
Man A

00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:46.550
A beam extends
towards RoboArisu

00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:46.550
Mad King Kai appears between 
RoboArisu and Magical Erika.

00:15:55.600 --> 00:15:59.570
President, it appears that the anime 
club's anime project is progressing.

00:15:59.570 --> 00:16:01.670
It's never going to turn out good.

00:16:03.020 --> 00:16:05.020
<b>Studio</b>

00:16:05.320 --> 00:16:07.020
<i>Is everyone here?</i>

00:16:07.020 --> 00:16:08.350
Yes.

00:16:08.350 --> 00:16:11.740
<i>The dubbing is the moment that the 
characters are brought to life.</i>

00:16:11.740 --> 00:16:13.280
<i>I'm counting on you.</i>

00:16:13.570 --> 00:16:15.530
I'm the magician?

00:16:15.530 --> 00:16:16.160
Yeah.

00:16:16.160 --> 00:16:18.070
Be your usual energetic self, Yui-chan.

00:16:18.070 --> 00:16:19.790
Neko-senpai, you do the meowing.

00:16:21.540 --> 00:16:26.170
Oh, yeah, Nakano-senpai, my sister had 
club work, so she couldn't make time.

00:16:26.560 --> 00:16:29.300
We can record her separately. Don't worry.

00:16:29.680 --> 00:16:33.290
Okay, why don't we go through the 
video to get a sense of the timing?

00:16:37.130 --> 00:16:38.250
Black and white?

00:16:38.250 --> 00:16:39.310
It is.

00:16:39.570 --> 00:16:43.810
The visuals aren't necessarily done 
by the time the dubbing happens.

00:16:44.260 --> 00:16:46.850
We're lucky we have rough art, even.

00:16:46.850 --> 00:16:48.760
Sometimes, when they don't have enough time,

00:16:48.760 --> 00:16:52.820
they have to record based on 
video made from the storyboards.

00:16:53.820 --> 00:16:58.440
Professional voice actors work with what 
they have to capture the characters' emotions

00:16:58.440 --> 00:17:00.580
and expressions to put on 
beautiful performances.

00:16:59.080 --> 00:17:02.080
Fuyuhiko

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:02.080
Amazing, huh?

00:17:02.400 --> 00:17:04.580
All right, here we go, the actual take.

00:17:10.310 --> 00:17:11.370
Here we go.

00:17:11.370 --> 00:17:13.590
Go, RoboArisu!

00:17:13.590 --> 00:17:15.990
Schwing!

00:17:15.990 --> 00:17:17.390
<i>Stop, stop.</i>

00:17:17.850 --> 00:17:20.190
<i>Arisu-chan, you're putting 
too much emotion into it.</i>

00:17:20.190 --> 00:17:21.710
<i>Try to be more mech-like.</i>

00:17:21.710 --> 00:17:24.280
With all due respect, I'm the main character.

00:17:24.280 --> 00:17:25.370
It needs to be emotional.

00:17:25.370 --> 00:17:26.890
<i>The robot isn't the main character.</i>

00:17:26.890 --> 00:17:27.860
<i>Once more.</i>

00:17:27.860 --> 00:17:29.650
B-But...

00:17:29.650 --> 00:17:31.370
Schwing!

00:17:31.370 --> 00:17:32.680
<i>That's too weak.</i>

00:17:34.240 --> 00:17:36.240
Not enough money.

00:17:36.240 --> 00:17:37.870
Not enough money.

00:17:38.350 --> 00:17:40.620
Heh, heh, it's morphin' time!

00:17:40.620 --> 00:17:41.930
<i>Stop, stop.</i>

00:17:42.310 --> 00:17:44.810
<i>Erika-senpai, you breathed on the mic.</i>

00:17:44.810 --> 00:17:46.880
<i>Watch out for the H-syllables.</i>

00:17:46.880 --> 00:17:48.290
<i>And Arisu-chan...</i>

00:17:48.290 --> 00:17:49.500
Me, again?

00:17:49.960 --> 00:17:52.690
Can you speak the G-syllables 
through your nose?

00:17:52.690 --> 00:17:53.630
Make them velar nasals.

00:17:53.840 --> 00:17:55.380
Velar nasals?

00:17:55.590 --> 00:17:59.040
It's a technique for making voiced G 
consonants sound pleasant to the ear.

00:17:59.040 --> 00:18:01.470
<i>I-I don't get it.</i>

00:18:01.470 --> 00:18:03.140
Not that "G."

00:18:05.220 --> 00:18:09.380
Behold, Kaikai Blade! I mean, Musashisakai—

00:18:09.380 --> 00:18:10.600
<i>Stop.</i>

00:18:10.600 --> 00:18:12.640
<i>We don't need your ad lib.</i>

00:18:13.160 --> 00:18:14.900
The humiliation!

00:18:17.300 --> 00:18:19.070
My name is Yuirin!

00:18:19.070 --> 00:18:22.370
I'm a magician that loves 
excitement and explosions!

00:18:22.370 --> 00:18:24.370
<i>Okay, you're good at this.</i>

00:18:24.370 --> 00:18:25.540
Thank you.

00:18:27.100 --> 00:18:29.040
Well, you <i>are</i> a guest.

00:18:29.290 --> 00:18:30.200
Meow.

00:18:30.810 --> 00:18:32.270
<i>Once more.</i>

00:18:32.270 --> 00:18:34.090
<i>Can you be more cat-like?</i>

00:18:35.420 --> 00:18:38.190
You're telling me to fly?

00:18:38.190 --> 00:18:41.180
Don't worry, we can do it.

00:18:41.180 --> 00:18:42.280
That was good!

00:18:42.280 --> 00:18:43.800
That was absolutely great!

00:18:43.800 --> 00:18:46.430
It was so good, do it again, thank you!

00:18:48.420 --> 00:18:51.870
The Earth is saved once again.

00:18:54.340 --> 00:18:56.250
<i>Okay, Minoa-chan.</i>

00:18:57.380 --> 00:18:58.820
It's over.

00:19:06.200 --> 00:19:10.830
Good Work
on the Dubbing

00:19:06.560 --> 00:19:08.390
Wh-What's this?

00:19:08.390 --> 00:19:10.830
It's one of those post-dubbing things.

00:19:11.200 --> 00:19:13.130
Good work, everyone.

00:19:13.130 --> 00:19:16.750
Now we need to match the art to the 
dialogue and add sound effects.

00:19:16.750 --> 00:19:18.760
We're getting close to the end.

00:19:18.760 --> 00:19:20.100
Oh, yeah.

00:19:20.100 --> 00:19:21.340
You're right.

00:19:21.780 --> 00:19:24.000
There's still work to do,

00:19:24.000 --> 00:19:27.600
but we're almost done making the 
anime, thanks to everyone's help.

00:19:27.760 --> 00:19:30.480
Now that we're done dubbing, 
we're picking up steam.

00:19:30.480 --> 00:19:32.080
We've won!

00:19:33.110 --> 00:19:35.320
Let's do this!

00:19:42.910 --> 00:19:44.120
One more scene.

00:19:44.680 --> 00:19:46.120
We just need one more scene.

00:19:47.380 --> 00:19:49.890
The ending theme <i>still</i> isn't done?

00:19:49.890 --> 00:19:52.120
We won't have it in time for editing!

00:19:52.680 --> 00:19:57.610
You're a failure of a creator 
if you can't meet deadlines.

00:19:55.850 --> 00:19:58.380
This doesn't look anything like my character.

00:19:58.650 --> 00:20:00.500
Do you have a problem with my art?

00:20:00.500 --> 00:20:01.600
Plenty.

00:20:01.600 --> 00:20:03.140
Do you want me to redo everything?

00:20:03.320 --> 00:20:05.540
Sorry, please, thank you, Arisu-chan.

00:20:09.250 --> 00:20:10.600
Just a little more.

00:20:12.410 --> 00:20:14.190
President, this is bad!

00:20:14.190 --> 00:20:17.400
The Anime Club's anime is nearing completion.

00:20:18.940 --> 00:20:20.030
I see.

00:20:20.240 --> 00:20:24.240
Inform all clubs to cease 
cooperation with the Anime Club.

00:20:24.240 --> 00:20:27.300
Should they resist, 
their clubs will be shut down.

00:20:27.710 --> 00:20:28.860
That's taking it too—

00:20:28.860 --> 00:20:32.540
I'm ordering you, as the 
student council president.

00:20:32.760 --> 00:20:34.990
Inform them immediately.

00:20:34.990 --> 00:20:36.060
O-Okay.

00:20:36.060 --> 00:20:38.420
Oh, one more thing.

00:20:43.180 --> 00:20:44.430
It looks good.

00:20:44.430 --> 00:20:46.880
Three more days until the school festival.

00:20:46.880 --> 00:20:48.410
I think we can make it!

00:20:48.820 --> 00:20:50.100
This is bad!

00:20:50.600 --> 00:20:51.910
Gomon-sensei...

00:20:51.910 --> 00:20:53.190
What about Gomon-sensei?

00:20:54.850 --> 00:20:55.940
Please don't look for me.

00:20:55.940 --> 00:20:58.190
The production assistant escapes?!

00:20:58.370 --> 00:20:59.940
It's one of those things.

00:21:00.220 --> 00:21:03.880
The concert band refuses 
to do the ending song.

00:21:03.880 --> 00:21:06.700
The broadcasting club says they can't lend
us the studio to record the remaining lines.

00:21:06.970 --> 00:21:08.910
What happened all of a sudden?

00:21:11.520 --> 00:21:13.710
I have a message for the Anime Club.

00:21:13.710 --> 00:21:16.710
We've prepared a special place for you.

00:21:19.820 --> 00:21:21.840
It's a special stage at the track field.

00:21:20.500 --> 00:21:23.460
B. Seating Area

00:21:21.840 --> 00:21:25.970
If you can't fill this up, we'll 
deem your presentation a failure.

00:21:23.470 --> 00:21:25.970
A. Special Stage

00:21:25.260 --> 00:21:25.970
<b>Sakaneko Academy Festival Venue</b>

00:21:29.070 --> 00:21:31.220
Tsubaki, why?

00:21:32.520 --> 00:21:36.510
I look forward to an amazing performance.

00:21:45.620 --> 00:21:49.600
There's no way the anime screening 
can fill the seats by itself.

00:21:50.510 --> 00:21:53.280
I think we might be out of options...

00:23:24.420 --> 00:23:26.940
I wish I had some lines.

00:23:26.940 --> 00:23:29.090
All I say is "meow."

00:23:29.090 --> 00:23:31.670
Of course, I gave it all I had.

00:23:31.670 --> 00:23:34.890
Next episode, calamity 
befalls the Anime Club.

00:23:34.890 --> 00:23:37.710
We're literally five seconds 
to dropping the anime.

00:23:37.710 --> 00:23:40.260
Just please, don't deliver 
the show on the day-of.
